Algorithms and constants followed

The Go implementation is this repository's own. To produce the same signals as
the reference implementation of the models it runs, it follows their published
preprocessing:

- The MiniFASNet crop (scale reduction, aspect-preserving enlargement, edge
  shifting, inclusive integer region), the 80x80 BGR raw-pixel input, the
  per-model crop scales 2.7 and 4.0, the class indices and the fusion of the
  two models' probabilities, as in minivision-ai/Silent-Face-Anti-Spoofing
  (https://github.com/minivision-ai/Silent-Face-Anti-Spoofing, Apache License
  2.0), and the ONNX export conventions of yakhyo/face-anti-spoofing (Apache
  License 2.0).
- The bilinear resize with pixel-centre alignment, as OpenCV's cv2.resize
  (https://github.com/opencv/opencv, Apache License 2.0) defines it.
- The 64-bit difference hash, a published, widely used perceptual-hash
  technique.

